.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local environment. Copying a .env into the image bakes the developer's
# APP_KEY and database password into a layer anyone with the image can read,
# and it would then override whatever the deployment injects at runtime.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Installed dependencies are rebuilt inside the image. Copying the host's
# vendor/ also copies its platform-specific binaries, which are wrong for the
# image's platform and break composer install in confusing ways.
vendor/
node_modules/

# Local developer state that must never reach a deployed image.
#
# storage/framework/ is excluded whole, not per-subdirectory. Live containers
# write here as root through the bind mount, so on the host these directories
# are owned by root - and Docker cannot even read the build context, let alone
# copy it, which fails the build with "open .../storage/framework/testing/disks:
# permission denied". Enumerating cache/sessions/views left testing/ behind and
# produced exactly that. The Dockerfile recreates the directories the app needs,
# so nothing here belongs in the context.
storage/framework/
storage/logs/
storage/app/imports/
storage/app/documents/
storage/app/attachments/
bootstrap/cache/*.php

# Front-end build state. public/build is compiled in the assets stage of the
# Dockerfile, so whatever a developer has locally is stale by definition - and
# public/hot, which `npm run dev` writes, would make Blade's @vite directive
# point the deployed image at a vite dev server on localhost that does not exist
# in the deployed stack. Neither file is committed, so neither belongs in a build
# context. Excluding public/build is also what makes the assets stage the only
# possible source of the assets that ship.
public/build/
public/hot

# The compiled agent binary is 150 MB and is gitignored on purpose. It is
# fetched by the agent download route at runtime, not baked into the image.
storage/app/agent/*.exe

# Local tooling output
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor directories
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp